Ticket #4471 says 412 reports were merged as one issue. The export contains 427 rows because its pages overlap; 15 report IDs repeat identically. Counting each ID once leaves 412 reports and **two causes**, not one.

## Shared parser reads day-first dates as month-first

**379 reports** across 11 tenants belong to this cause. It includes app and email reports and booking-v2 form reports. The shared parser reads every date month-first even though these tenants use day-first locales, so day and month values flip. For example, R-41200 says a 7 April reminder went out on 4 July.

## booking-v3 hint conflicts with tenant date order

**33 reports** belong to this cause, all from booking forms at copper.studio, alder.physio, and pale.harbour. booking-v3 displays `MM/DD/YYYY`, but the form interprets dates in the tenant's day-first order. People follow the hint and the form reads a different date. For example, R-41230 says a client came on 1 June instead of 6 January.

## Triage

Use the report ID to deduplicate overlapping export pages, then classify using the tenant locale, channel, and form version. The intake tag and subject line are not reliable cause labels: reports in each cause carry both intake tags, and many different subjects occur in both groups. The five reports noted as one-day moves remain in the parser group under this classification; they do not form a third cause in the export's cause logic.

